startup log not captured
state: MISSING
reason: CATALINA_LOG is unset or does not name a readable file
configured-value: <unset>

THIS IS A GAP IN THE EVIDENCE, NOT AN OPTIONAL EXTRA.

The container log is the ONLY place three things can be observed, and
each of them is load-bearing for a claim this migration makes:
  * the startup frontend build, which is the one and only place the
    runtime package-manager wiring executes.  The frontend pipeline is
    invoked at container startup and not by the build, so without this
    log there is no evidence whatever that the migrated wiring runs the
    lockfile-respecting clean install rather than the superseded package
    manager it replaced.  A capture missing this log cannot support the
    claim that the frontend genuinely runs on the new runtime.
  * process-engine initialisation and the loading of every process
    definition, which is where flow 7 residual risk is discharged or
    left standing.
  * every ERROR and SEVERE line, without which a regression can hide
    behind a healthy readiness probe and a set of 200 responses.

Supply CATALINA_LOG pointing at the container log for both runs.  Until
then the startup-derived observations in flows 5 and 7 record this
unavailability explicitly rather than asserting anything about a log that
was never read, and no claim about the startup frontend build may be
made from this capture.
